        "Close to home, the district has Sri Krishnadevaraya University and JNTU Anantapur at Anantapur, the Central University of Andhra Pradesh and a government medical college, while Vijayanagara Sri Krishnadevaraya University in Ballari is a bus ride across the border. Those institutions mostly recruit through State Board and entrance-exam routes, so an IB or IGCSE student applying to them should check the equivalence paperwork and the counselling rules published each year instead of assuming the same path as a classmate.",
        "The Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence for foreign qualifications: the IB Diploma is treated as equal to Class 12 and the IGCSE as equal to Class 10, subject to its conditions. JEE Main and NEET-UG publish their own eligibility rules on subject combinations and minimum marks, and a Diploma student who wants engineering needs Mathematics and Physics at a suitable level with Chemistry, while one who wants medicine needs Biology and Chemistry in the mix. These choices are made in Class 11, so asking early is worth it.",
        "Study abroad depends mostly on the predicted grade a school submits in the autumn of the final year, not on the May result. UK universities usually want a points total with named Higher Level subjects, US colleges weigh the predicted grade alongside essays and tests, and others apply their own conversions. A tutor's job is the subject depth and exam technique behind those predictions, not the applications, and we say so plainly rather than promise outcomes.",
