        "The two Mathematics courses suit different futures. Analysis and Approaches is for algebra, calculus and proof, and is the usual choice for engineering, physics or economics; its Higher Level adds a third paper made of long problems that cannot be solved by pattern-matching. Applications and Interpretation leans on statistics, modelling and technology, and suits biology, psychology, business and social science routes. In both, the Mathematics exploration counts for a fifth of the grade, and its biggest risk is leaving the topic until Class 12 is half over.",
        "Physics, Chemistry and Biology were redesigned for first examination in 2025, so students now meet structure and reactivity in Chemistry or space, time and motion in Physics, and a scientific investigation worth 20 percent. Practical work is the catch for a student without an IB school lab. A tutor can help design a feasible investigation, check the method for validity and discuss the analysis, but the experiment itself has to be carried out and authenticated through the school that holds the candidate registration.",
        "Students from State Board backgrounds typically arrive strong on content and weaker on command terms. An answer to explain earns marks for linked reasoning, one to evaluate needs a judgement with evidence for and against, and a data question expects units, uncertainty and a conclusion tied to the numbers. Sessions therefore alternate between a short concept and a long exam-style question, with the mark scheme beside the student's own answer.",
        "Groundnut, water and drought give this district real case material. A Biology or Environmental Systems student can ground answers in soil moisture and crop physiology, Chemistry in fertiliser, soil pH and water hardness, Geography in groundwater and dry-land farming. Examples a student has actually seen make answers specific, and they stick in memory better than a generic textbook illustration. A tutor can build a practice question around such an example, then show how the same answer would be marked against the command term in a real paper.",
